{
  "dom_id": "step-q60454",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Sophia bought $14$ peaches for $$4.$ What is the price per peach?",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of dollars to peaches is $4:14.$ Expressing this as a fraction, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{14}\n$$\n\nWe can reduce this fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4÷2}{14÷2}=\\frac{2}{7}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the price of each peach is $\\frac{2}{7}$ of one dollar.",
